      "message": "LGTM. In an RTL run the hard break sits at the lowest glyph index, so dropping it from the\nleft edge matches the paint path, and the split-grapheme path stays consistent with the main\npath. Placing the empty break box at the visual left edge also puts the caret on the logical\nend of the line.\n\nI also checked a few RTL edge cases locally on top of PS1, and all of them pass (they fail on\nthe parent): a hard break after a mark inside a grapheme (dal + fatha), after a lam-alef\nligature (including a range that cuts the ligature), after RTL trailing spaces, CRLF, empty RTL\nlines, mixed BiDi, letter and word spacing, and all text aligns with RectWidthStyle::kMax.\n\nTested: dm SkParagraph 236/236, Flutter framework corpus and web CanvasKit suite with no\nregressions, google3 paragraph tests with no regressions, txt_benchmarks neutral, ASAN bot green.",
